Translation patch: potentially_fix_state_incorrectly_encoded_by_libcrux_issue_1275 (spqr::incremental_mlkem768)

Change: the function is removed from the Charon `opaque` list in Cargo.toml, so its body is
extracted. The `log::info!` and `log::warn!` calls are commented out. Each 2-byte word is read
with `u16::from_le_bytes` instead of `i16::from_le_bytes`, and the patterns are the same bit
patterns as `u16` literals (`NEG1_I16` is `0xFFFF`, `NEG2_I16_GOOD` is `0xFFFE`, `NEG2_I16_BAD`
is `0xFEFF`); the three constants are commented out.
Why: `log` is excluded from the translation; its macros make Aeneas fail ("Internal error").
Aeneas emits negative `i16` literal patterns as `(-1)#iscalar`, which Lean's match compiler
rejects ("Failed to compile pattern matching").
Behaviour: identical apart from logging (no log output). `u16` and `i16` read the same two
bytes, and each pattern matches the same bit pattern as before, so every word takes the same
branch.

